From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher A. Williamson <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Disable SELinux flags kernel support notification

The GSI does not ship a GrapheneOS-patched kernel so the custom
SELinux flags proc attribute will never be present. The framework
already gracefully disables the affected hardening features when the
kernel lacks support, but still posts a persistent notification on
every boot for debuggable builds. Remove the notification since it is
expected and not actionable on a GSI.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000007
---
 .../com/android/server/ext/SystemServerExt.java    | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/ext/SystemServerExt.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/ext/SystemServerExt.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/ext/SystemServerExt.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/ext/SystemServerExt.java
@@ -38,14 +38,6 @@
     void initBgThread() {
         WifiAutoOff.maybeInit(this);
         BluetoothAutoOff.maybeInit(this);
-
-        if (Build.IS_DEBUGGABLE) {
-            if (!SELinuxFlags.kernelSupportsSELinuxFlags()) {
-                String title = "Kernel doesn't support SELinux flags";
-                String msg = "App hardening features that use SELinux flags, such as DCL and ptrace restrictions, do not work.";
-                new SystemErrorNotification("missing hardening", title, msg).show(context);
-            }
-        }
     }
 }
